{"answer": "The OpenTelemetry metrics API has no proxy meter, unlike its tracing API. An instrument created with `metrics.getMeter()` before a `MeterProvider` is registered is therefore a permanent no-op. It stays a no-op even if a provider is registered later. Lore's `libs/server-core/src/outbound/otel.ts` created its instruments at import time, and the entrypoint imported that file before `initOtel()` ran. So `lore.http.requests`, `lore.tool.calls` and the other counters never recorded anything. The fix (ADR-050, PR #2652) moved the instruments to `libs/shared/src/outbound/otel/metrics.ts`. They are now resolved lazily against the global meter provider at record time and memoized per provider.", "sources": ["adrs/ADR-050-prometheus-grafana-metrics.md", "Pull request #2652 in re-cinq/lore"]}
```

